Feature: Transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 bucket to Purgo S3 folder

  The Databricks PySpark script transfers files from the Vendor S3 bucket to the Purgo S3 folder based on the following rules:
  - Only files listed in the Vendor S3 folder (path from ingest_config_master.s3_vendor_path) are considered.
  - Files must not exist in either the Purgo S3 folder (ingest_config_master.s3_landing_path) or the Archive S3 folder (ingest_config_master.s3_archive_path).
  - Only files with active_flag = 'A' in ingest_config_master are eligible.
  - S3 folder paths are retrieved from ingest_config_master: s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, s3_archive_path.
  - AWS credentials are retrieved from Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" (keys: "access_key", "secret_key").
  - The script operates in Unity Catalog: purgo_databricks, Schema: purgo_playground.

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is set to "purgo_databricks"
    And the Schema is set to "purgo_playground"
    And the AWS credentials "access_key" and "secret_key" are retrieved from Databricks secret scope "aws_keys"
    And the ingest_config_master table is used for configuration
    And the S3 folder paths are retrieved from ingest_config_master columns: s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, s3_archive_path

  Scenario Outline: Transfer eligible active files from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3 folder (happy path)
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id     | <config_id>     |
      | file_name     | <file_name>     |
      | s3_vendor_path| <s3_vendor_path>|
      | s3_landing_path| <s3_landing_path>|
      | s3_archive_path| <s3_archive_path>|
      | active_flag   | A               |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" does not exist in the Purgo S3 folder at "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" does not exist in the Archive S3 folder at "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is transferred from "<s3_vendor_path>" to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" is not present in "<s3_vendor_path>" if vendor_file_deletion_flag = 'Y'
    And the transfer is logged with status "SUCCESS" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG001    | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder1/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |
      | CFG002    | report_20240602.txt| s3://vendor-bucket/folder2/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer inactive files (active_flag != 'A')
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id     | <config_id>     |
      | file_name     | <file_name>     |
      | s3_vendor_path| <s3_vendor_path>|
      | s3_landing_path| <s3_landing_path>|
      | s3_archive_path| <s3_archive_path>|
      | active_flag   | <inactive_flag> |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is not transferred to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SKIPPED" and reason "Inactive config" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | inactive_flag |
      | CFG003    | old_20230501.csv  | s3://vendor-bucket/folder3/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | I            |
      | CFG004    | test_20230401.txt | s3://vendor-bucket/folder4/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | N            |

  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer files already present in Purgo S3 folder
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id     | <config_id>     |
      | file_name     | <file_name>     |
      | s3_vendor_path| <s3_vendor_path>|
      | s3_landing_path| <s3_landing_path>|
      | s3_archive_path| <s3_archive_path>|
      | active_flag   | A               |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Purgo S3 folder at "<s3_landing_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is not transferred to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SKIPPED" and reason "File already exists in Purgo S3" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG005    | duplicate_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder5/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer files already present in Archive S3 folder
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id     | <config_id>     |
      | file_name     | <file_name>     |
      | s3_vendor_path| <s3_vendor_path>|
      | s3_landing_path| <s3_landing_path>|
      | s3_archive_path| <s3_archive_path>|
      | active_flag   | A               |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Archive S3 folder at "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is not transferred to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SKIPPED" and reason "File already exists in Archive S3" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG006    | archived_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder6/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  Scenario Outline: Error when AWS credentials are missing
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain "<missing_key>"
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Missing AWS credential: <missing_key>"
    And no files are transferred

    Examples:
      | missing_key  |
      | access_key   |
      | secret_key   |

  Scenario Outline: Error when S3 folder path is missing in ingest_config_master
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id     | <config_id>     |
      | file_name     | <file_name>     |
      | s3_vendor_path| <vendor_path>   |
      | s3_landing_path| <landing_path> |
      | s3_archive_path| <archive_path> |
      | active_flag   | A               |
    And the value "<missing_column>" is null or empty
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Missing S3 folder path: <missing_column>"
    And no files are transferred

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | vendor_path                  | landing_path                  | archive_path                  | missing_column   |
      | CFG007    | missing_vendor.csv|                              | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/    | s3_vendor_path   |
      | CFG008    | missing_landing.csv| s3://vendor-bucket/folder7/ |                               | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/    | s3_landing_path  |
      | CFG009    | missing_archive.csv| s3://vendor-bucket/folder8/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/    |                               | s3_archive_path  |

  Scenario Outline: Error when file transfer fails due to S3 access issues
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id     | <config_id>     |
      | file_name     | <file_name>     |
      | s3_vendor_path| <s3_vendor_path>|
      | s3_landing_path| <s3_landing_path>|
      | s3_archive_path| <s3_archive_path>|
      | active_flag   | A               |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the script cannot access "<s3_vendor_path>" or "<s3_landing_path>" due to permission error
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "S3 access denied for path: <error_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "FAILED" and reason "S3 access denied" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | error_path                  |
      | CFG010    | access_error.csv  | s3://vendor-bucket/folder9/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | s3://vendor-bucket/folder9/ |
      | CFG011    | landing_error.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder10/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/  |

  Scenario Outline: File transfer is recursive if file_recursive_flag = 'Y'
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id         | <config_id>         |
      | file_name         | <file_name>         |
      | s3_vendor_path    | <s3_vendor_path>    |
      | s3_landing_path   | <s3_landing_path>   |
      | s3_archive_path   | <s3_archive_path>   |
      | active_flag       | A                   |
      | file_recursive_flag| Y                  |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in a subfolder of "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" does not exist in "<s3_landing_path>" or "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is transferred from the subfolder of "<s3_vendor_path>" to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SUCCESS" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG012    | nested_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder11/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  Scenario Outline: File transfer is not recursive if file_recursive_flag != 'Y'
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id         | <config_id>         |
      | file_name         | <file_name>         |
      | s3_vendor_path    | <s3_vendor_path>    |
      | s3_landing_path   | <s3_landing_path>   |
      | s3_archive_path   | <s3_archive_path>   |
      | active_flag       | A                   |
      | file_recursive_flag| <recursive_flag>   |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in a subfolder of "<s3_vendor_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is not transferred to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SKIPPED" and reason "Recursive transfer not enabled" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | recursive_flag |
      | CFG013    | nested_20240602.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder12/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | N             |
      | CFG014    | nested_20240603.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder13/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |               |

  Scenario Outline: File transfer with vendor_file_deletion_flag = 'Y'
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id         | <config_id>         |
      | file_name         | <file_name>         |
      | s3_vendor_path    | <s3_vendor_path>    |
      | s3_landing_path   | <s3_landing_path>   |
      | s3_archive_path   | <s3_archive_path>   |
      | active_flag       | A                   |
      | vendor_file_deletion_flag| Y            |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" does not exist in "<s3_landing_path>" or "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is transferred from "<s3_vendor_path>" to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" is deleted from "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SUCCESS" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                |
      | CFG015    | delete_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder14/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |

  Scenario Outline: File transfer with vendor_file_deletion_flag != 'Y'
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id         | <config_id>         |
      | file_name         | <file_name>         |
      | s3_vendor_path    | <s3_vendor_path>    |
      | s3_landing_path   | <s3_landing_path>   |
      | s3_archive_path   | <s3_archive_path>   |
      | active_flag       | A                   |
      | vendor_file_deletion_flag| <deletion_flag>|
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" does not exist in "<s3_landing_path>" or "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is transferred from "<s3_vendor_path>" to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" remains in "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SUCCESS" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | deletion_flag |
      | CFG016    | keep_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder15/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | N            |
      | CFG017    | keep_20240602.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder16/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     |              |

  Scenario Outline: File transfer with file name validation
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id         | <config_id>         |
      | file_name         | <file_name>         |
      | s3_vendor_path    | <s3_vendor_path>    |
      | s3_landing_path   | <s3_landing_path>   |
      | s3_archive_path   | <s3_archive_path>   |
      | active_flag       | A                   |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file name "<file_name>" matches the pattern "<file_name_pattern>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is transferred from "<s3_vendor_path>" to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "SUCCESS" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | file_name_pattern         |
      | CFG018    | valid_20240601.csv| s3://vendor-bucket/folder17/  | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | ^[a-zA-Z0-9_\-]+\.csv$   |

  Scenario Outline: Error when file name does not match expected pattern
    Given ingest_config_master contains a row with
      | config_id         | <config_id>         |
      | file_name         | <file_name>         |
      | s3_vendor_path    | <s3_vendor_path>    |
      | s3_landing_path   | <s3_landing_path>   |
      | s3_archive_path   | <s3_archive_path>   |
      | active_flag       | A                   |
    And the file "<file_name>" exists in the Vendor S3 folder at "<s3_vendor_path>"
    And the file name "<file_name>" does not match the pattern "<file_name_pattern>"
    When the script is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid file name format: <file_name>"
    And the transfer is logged with status "FAILED" and reason "Invalid file name format" in s3_file_process_log

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name         | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | file_name_pattern         |
      | CFG019    | invalid@20240601.csv| s3://vendor-bucket/folder18/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/     | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/     | ^[a-zA-Z0-9_\-]+\.csv$   |

  Scenario: No eligible files to transfer
    Given ingest_config_master contains only inactive configs or all files in Vendor S3 exist in Purgo or Archive S3 folders
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred
    And a log entry is created with status "NO FILES TO TRANSFER" in s3_file_process_log

  Scenario: File transfer atomicity
    Given a file "atomic_20240601.csv" is eligible for transfer
    When the script is executed
    Then the file is marked as transferred only after successful copy to "<s3_landing_path>"
    And if the transfer fails, the file is not marked as transferred
    And the transfer is logged with status "SUCCESS" or "FAILED" in s3_file_process_log

  Scenario: File format validation
    Given ingest_config_master specifies expected file format as ".csv"
    And the file "wrongformat_20240601.txt" exists in Vendor S3 folder
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "wrongformat_20240601.txt" is not transferred
    And the transfer is logged with status "SKIPPED" and reason "File format not allowed" in s3_file_process_log

  Scenario: Logging of all transfer attempts
    Given multiple files are processed for transfer
    When the script is executed
    Then each file transfer attempt is logged in s3_file_process_log with file_name, s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, s3_archive_path, file_status, and file_processed_date

  Scenario: Scheduled batch job execution
    Given the script is scheduled to run as a batch job
    When the scheduled time is reached
    Then the script executes all eligible file transfers as per the above scenarios

  Scenario: Event-triggered execution
    Given the script is triggered by an event (e.g., new file arrival in Vendor S3)
    When the event occurs
    Then the script executes all eligible file transfers as per the above scenarios
